# Counter

`actor.ts` defines the Counter aggregate, Increment and Decrement commands, native replies, owner authorization and a committed-event notification policy. Positive even counts start a native Effect workflow and checkpoint its notification Activity. `notifyLayer` supplies the external notification implementation. There is no model provider or API key.

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set `TARDIGRADE_TOKEN` and `TARDIGRADE_SUBJECT`. Run `bun run dev` for the Alchemy Cloudflare platform. The counter uses native Domain Durable Objects and native Effect workflow checkpoints. `bun run dev:memory` runs the example with ephemeral memory state; its state and workflow results end with the process.

Use `bun run cli --help` for commands and reads generated from CounterApi. Increment and Decrement use the same immutable counter ID. A caller-supplied command ID retries its original native receipt. Reads and receipt replay require the owning subject. Notifications have at-least-once external delivery; a process failure after an external effect and before its Activity checkpoint can repeat that effect.

Keep decisions in the aggregate and external work in the native workflow Activity. `worker.ts` and `alchemy.run.ts` own hosting. Preview with `bun run plan:cloudflare` and deploy with `bun run deploy:cloudflare`. Existing actor journals require an explicit import before cutover.
